# Target C-II — collapsed support-six blocks consume at least eleven strict rhombi

**Date:** 2026-09-22  
**Claim class:** exact finite/global train-topology strengthening; theorem-state authority unchanged  
**Scope:** degree-pure collapsed support-six one-anchor components after maximal two-anchor activation  
**Depends on:** the audited weights-through-nine certificate, the audited 388-cell / 42-orbit rotation census, the exact MI.1 cycle equations, strict crossing-angle difference constraints, the forced crossing rotations, and exhaustive planarization  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_support6_collapsed_eleven_crossing_floor_2026_09_22.cpp`  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The collapsed support-six endpoint has twelve internal relation trains. Let (X_K) be
the number of strict-rhombus crossings whose two complete trains are both internal
to one collapsed block (K). The prior exact finite certificate excluded weights
(0,ldots,9), proving (X_Kge10). The present run extends the same necessary
condition search to weight ten and finds no planar candidate:

\[
\boxed{X_K\ge 11.}
\tag{TC.1}
\]

This is a global statement about any planar stopped-train realization of the block.
It does not assert that eleven crossings are realizable, and it does not use the
nonlinear six-face closure equations.

## Exact finite certificate

The verifier reconstructs the 388 rational rotation cells (180 all-cross and 208
mixed) and their 42 sign-preserving symmetry representatives. For every representative
and every selected internal train-pair set of cardinality (10), it performs the
following exact tests:

1. solve the complete MI.1 affine system over (mathbb F_2);
2. retain only triangle-free crossing assignments;
3. enumerate every orientation of every selected strict crossing window
   \[
   1<x_e-x_f<2\quad\text{or}\quad1<x_f-x_e<2;
   \]
4. impose all selected windows simultaneously on the same strict rational difference
   cell; and
5. planarize every selected crossing with its geometrically forced cyclic rotation
   and enumerate every order of multiple selected crossings along every train.

The strict difference feasibility test is the exact integer-scaled Bellman--Ford
criterion used by the audited weights-through-nine certificate. The planarization test
uses Euler characteristic; positive genus for every order is a necessary-condition
exclusion.

The complete aggregate output of the new weight-ten pass is

```text
TOTAL k=10 parity=58377 tri=40324 metric=20349 planar=0
PASS: no collapsed support-six symmetry orbit admits a planar, angle-compatible MI.1 crossing pattern with 10 internal crossings.
```

Here `parity` counts all MI.1 survivors, `tri` applies the necessary triangle-free
condition, `metric` counts assignments with at least one simultaneous orientation of
all strict crossing windows, and `planar` counts assignments for which some
crossing-order permutation has genus zero. The final count is zero in both matching
types and every one of the 42 representatives; the displayed total is the sum of
the 42 per-representative rows emitted by the verifier.

The representative quotient is safe in the excluding direction: every labelled cell
is the image of a representative under a sign-preserving relabeling and/or reflection,
and the MI.1 equations, strict angle windows, forced crossing sign, and genus are
transported by that symmetry. No floating-point decision occurs.

## Global strict-rhombus payment

Distinct collapsed one-anchor components have disjoint internal relation-train sets.
Since a strict rhombus belongs to exactly two complete trains, an internal crossing
rhombus counted by one component cannot be counted by another. If (c_6) is the
number of active collapsed support-six components and (R_4) is the total strict-
rhombus population, summing (TC.1) gives

\[
\boxed{R_4\ge11c_6,\qquad c_6\le R_4/11.}
\tag{TC.2}
\]

Combining this with the independently audited tangent payment

\[
d_C\ge M_0+2c_6
\]

gives the safe two-currency bound

\[
\boxed{
c_6\le
\min\left\{\frac{d_C-M_0}{2},\frac{R_4}{11}\right\}.
}
\tag{TC.3}
\]

In the existing support accounting, where a collapsed block contributes (c_6/7) to
the support-six term, this replaces the prior (R_4/70) arm by (R_4/77). This is a
strict finite strengthening, but its asymptotic effect is only a linear payment in
the number of collapsed blocks while the near-extremal rhombus population can be
quadratic.

## Scope and remaining obstruction

The theorem does not close C-II. It rules out every weight-ten internal crossing set
under the audited necessary conditions; weights (11+) are not searched because the
current certificate does not need them for (TC.1), and an eleven-crossing floor would
require excluding only weight ten after the prior weights-through-nine theorem. The
live continuation is to extract a boundary, train-order, or diameter-locking charge
from the eleven-or-more forced crossings, or to combine (TC.2) with the actual
terminal/FREE inequalities without discarding its correlation with (d_C).

**Disposition:** proved candidate awaiting independent audit; exact certificate passes;
canonical theorem state unchanged; C-II remains open.
